{"ts":"2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9b054e739855a3b67742faac","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-a8zm","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Task lifecycle\n\n- A qualifying operation may return a durable task handle when the tasks extension is negotiated.\n- tasks/get polls authoritative status, bounded progress, result, error, expiration, and recovery.\n- tasks/update supplies mid-flight client input and composes with MRTR without two conflicting state machines.\n- Cancellation and timeout are idempotent and terminal task states are immutable events.\n- Handles are scoped to workspace, authority, protocol policy, and retention; they never expose filesystem paths or secrets.\n- Existing pm plan, test-run, telemetry, and history identifiers remain domain records and are not silently conflated with transport task handles."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rzs24j"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Official MCP tasks extension for pm: asynchronous long operations, tasks/get polling, tasks/update input, durable handles, and lifecycle convergence"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Expose long-running pm operations through io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks with SDK-owned durable handles, polling, mid-flight input, cancellation, expiration, and immutable lifecycle evidence."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:mcp","area:sdk","async","durable-handles","long-running","tasks-extension"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/deadline","value":"2026-11-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":900},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The tasks extension is explicitly negotiated and never appears as an unadvertised core capability; Eligible long operations can return durable handles without per-request opt-in and tasks/get reports bounded authoritative state; tasks/update accepts validated mid-flight input and composes deterministically with MRTR inputResponses; tasks/list and blocking tasks/result are not implemented on the canonical 2026-07-28 path; Cancellation, duplicate updates, expiration, unauthorized access, restart recovery, retention, and immutable terminal evidence have negative tests; The SDK provides a transport-neutral task provider and adapters for test, reindex, graph, import, and validation operations"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"Standard asynchronous execution for long pm operations"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Map tests, reindexing, graph analysis, imports, validation, and other bounded long operations onto the official tasks extension"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Hosts can start, inspect, steer, cancel, and recover long pm work without blocking a request or inventing a private job protocol"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"2026-07-28 moves tasks out of core and redesigns them around tasks/get, tasks/update, unsolicited handles, and extension negotiation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-rs9vry"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-klxax7","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-qd6gvf","kind":"verifies","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-rz9gep","kind":"blocked_by","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-x705zo","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-25T05:09:28.783Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks tasks/get tasks/update tasks/result tasks/list durable handles polling and mid-flight input. Existing pm task and plan items are domain lifecycle work and do not implement the MCP extension."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"099f3e45809d6e6416cb0cb69527877fb01c15479fb7bc4328835d685802e8eb","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
